# vaxis (Zag third_party)

Upstream: https://github.com/rockorager/vaxis v0.6.0 (MIT, see LICENSE)

Source: copied verbatim from the vendored copy at
`pi-mono-zig/zig/vendor/vaxis` (its checkout of vaxis 0.6.0, zig 0.16
std.Io-era), commit state as of 2026-08-06. Read-only: never edit these
files; changes come from upstream.

Zag: path-vendored under `packages/third_party/vaxis`; imported ONLY into
the `zag-tui` module graph (`-Dtui=true`). Hard imports `zigimg` + `uucode`
resolve from the local zig cache (offline; tarballs already present).

Deviation from upstream `src/tty.zig` (PosixTty only, marked
"Zag deviation (tui-vaxis-001)" in the source): `Tty.init` prefers the stdin
terminal when stdin is a tty, falling back to `/dev/tty`. Upstream opens
only `/dev/tty` (the controlling terminal); zag's terminal contract is
stdin/stdout-based and the PTY process fixture runs the child WITHOUT a
controlling terminal (macOS teardown constraint), where `/dev/tty` would
resolve to the test runner's terminal instead of the PTY slave. A matching
`owned_fd` guard keeps deinit from closing a borrowed stdin fd. Everything
else is byte-identical to the pi-mono-zig vendored copy.

Bump: replace the directory from the upstream release (or the pi-mono-zig
vendored copy), re-apply the two PosixTty deviation hunks above, keep
LICENSE + build.zig + build.zig.zon + src/, and re-run the four zag matrices
including `-Dtui=true`.
